## Lehi assassinates 5 members of Shubaki Family.

The assassination was premeditated as a reprisal for for Shubaki family allegedly providing information to the British that led to the capture of Lehi members.

---
id: 1947-11-29-un-partition-plan
when: 1947-11-29
actors: [un]
---
## UN Partition Plan

The United Nations General Assembly adopted Resolution 181 (II), which recommended the adoption and implementation of a Plan of Partition with Economic Union.

---
id: 1947-11-30-arab-militants-belonging-to-the
when: 1947-11-30
actors: [un]  # auto-tagged from text: un
---
## Arab militants belonging to the Abu Qishq gang attack Jewish buses, killing 7.

Flyers appearing afterwards claimed the attack was in retaliation for the Shubaki family assassination. It's later reported to Ben Gurion that the attacks were unrelated to the UN Resolution.

---
id: 1947-12-01-irgun-and-haganah-begin-urban
when: 1947-12-01
where: [haifa]  # TODO(migration): matched from the title; verify
actors: [haganah, palmach, irgun]  # auto-tagged from text: haganah, palmach, irgun
---
## Irgun and Haganah begin urban terror campaign against 75,000 Palestinians in Haifa.

Special units of the Haganah comprising of undercover operatives, called mistravim (becoming Arab), use sniper and machine gun fire and barrel bombs to terrorize Arab neighborhoods. The official historian of the Palmach surmises: 'The Palestinians [in Haifa] were from December onwards under siege and intimidation.'

---
